WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.690
So Ra No Wo To

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:50.100
That noise would wake the dead.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.110
A Day with the Squad -
Rio Runs

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.180
Let's eat!

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.400
How is it?

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.920
It's pretty good.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.100
Yeah. This is yummy.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.580
Well, it's not bad.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.960
Great!

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.330
It's a dish native to my village.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:27.160
Is this "miso" the stuff that's
made the same way as soy?

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:27.870
Yes.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.930
I brought a bit of miso
my mom made.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.480
There's plenty more,

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.280
so eat up!

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.610
To Treize?

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:42.780
Yeah.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.080
We finally received notification
about more supplies.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.790
I'm taking Kureha-chan
to pick them up.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:56.130
We're running low on ammunition, medicine,
and a lot of everyday supplies, right?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.960
We'll be all right now!

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.400
And Noël?

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.910
Carl-san's studio, right?

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:04.990
Got it.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.290
Kanata!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.310
We're spending the whole
afternoon practicing!

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.320
Really?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.700
Grub's ready.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.980
What horrible manners...

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.110
Your dad would cry
if he saw that.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.530
Like I care.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.710
Here, have a snack.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.270
Fortune cookies?

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.790
You don't like them, huh?

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.200
It isn't the kids at the
church's fault.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.550
Demanding money to spread
their useless superstitions...

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.140
It's the same as everywhere else.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:32.510
Oh, that's not true at all.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.680
These are good cookies!

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:39.560
Oh, my!

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.590
<b>Good Luck</b>

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:51.580
She seems like she's
really fitting in.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.660
It's cute how hard
she always tries.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.210
You think?

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.380
I'll admit she's serious
and fired-up.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:03.670
But things out here aren't easy enough
to get by on those qualities alone.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.060
What does that look mean?

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.040
It's a secret!

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.280
What?

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.780
That's annoying.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.590
<b>Horrible Luck</b>

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.850
All right, see you guys.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.600
I'll be back late.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.020
OK. Be careful.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.100
Don't cause trouble
for Rio-sempai.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.210
Setting sail...

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.250
Bye-bye!

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.580
I don't expect you to
be able to do this,

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.250
but you should be able to control the
sound using only the mouthpiece.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:03.730
Try it!

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:09.910
O-OK!

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.900
How are you finding
life at the base?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.540
It's fun!

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.590
You're so easygoing
about everything.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.180
I'm a bit jealous.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.930
Come to think of it,
why did you join the army?

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:35.580
You see...

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:40.610
I... I heard I could learn to
play an instrument for free...

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:47.010
But I understand that p-protecting
the country is important!

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:51.580
I don't care whether it was
for money or whatever...

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:57.590
Those with a distinct goal in mind last longer
than those who just kind of joined up.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.960
Um... Thank you.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.920
Then, why did you join, Rio-sempai?

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:09.820
I...

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.460
Yeah...

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:14.100
I guess for the opposite
of your reason.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.350
But that's rare these days.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:22.980
You almost never hear brass instruments
outside of the military.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.310
I heard it a long time ago...

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.120
A sound like yours, Sempai.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:31.280
Kanata?

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.830
A sound of the sky...

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.340
What's wrong?

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.450
Wake up!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.040
Wake up, Kanata!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.240
Answer me!

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.290
No!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.240
Just stay still.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:11.210
It's hot. It's hot, Mom...

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.180
Are you hot?

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.780
OK... It's OK.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:16.160
You're OK.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:27.330
Mom... Mom...

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.060
What's wrong, Kanata?

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.590
Kanata!

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.350
I want some snow to eat...

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.970
OK. Just wait!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:53.160
Snow... Where's the snow...

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.320
Why the hell would we
have any snow?!

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:00.530
Calm down.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:01.720
Calm down...

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:04.790
Medicine!

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.300
No. That's a last resort!

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.130
Medicine, medicine...

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.540
Medicine! Medicine...

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:28.690
Found it!

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.110
<i>...running low on a
lot of stuff, right?</i>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.950
Damn those idiots in
the Supply Corps!

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.440
Damn.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:46.630
What should I do...

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.930
Damn it all!

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.970
Um... Did you need something?

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.670
Did the children cause
problems again?

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.530
Please forgive me for my rudeness
up until this point.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:14.020
So, um...

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:16.050
Save her!

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:29.490
Drink this.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:31.820
Good girl.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:43.240
She's got a bit of high fever,
but this should do it.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.700
Is it something really bad?

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.560
I think it's malaria.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:52.240
Malaria? Only kids get that.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:57.720
Even adults can get it
if they're very tired.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:05.760
A lot of kids get it right
after we take them in.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:10.470
The more they appear to be fine,
the worse it is when it hits.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.490
She was fighting it off the whole time, I bet.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:18.660
Th-Then... Will she get better?

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:19.980
She won't stay like this forever, right?

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.520
I think she'll be fine.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:28.450
I'm so glad.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:33.860
Thank you...

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:36.460
Uh...

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:39.960
My name is Yumina.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.490
This is infused with herbs.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.970
Give it to her a little later.

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:58.120
Uh, thank you for everything.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.060
Don't worry about it.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:06.530
Serving the people of this town
is our joy and our duty.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:11.620
May all blessings be upon you.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.190
Thank you for your cooperation!

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:12.960
Ow.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:18.130
I-I'm sorry!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.990
You OK?

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.380
I'm sorry.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.150
I'm an <i>omiso</i>.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:38.770
The stuff we had this morning?

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:39.960
No.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.120
Miso dregs...

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.530
When you make miso soup,
you strain the miso...

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:48.650
The leftover beans,
and stuff from it.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:52.360
Good-for-nothing, useless,

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.580
like that...

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:57.280
I've always been like that,
ever since I was a kid.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:03.880
So I thought that this time, I'd work
really hard and not trouble anyone.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:05.970
But...

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:12.320
You were a lot more fragile
than you looked.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:16.100
And a selfish, spoiled kid...

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:23.360
Did... Did I say something?

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.480
A lot of stuff!

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:36.910
Oh, sempai!

00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:38.970
What?

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:41.420
That song you were singing...

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.390
What are you talking about?

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:46.540
This song.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.000
Amazing.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:05.030
She only heard it one time.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:06.830
It wasn't the first
time I'd heard it.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.150
I heard it a long time ago.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:14.690
I always wanted to play it myself.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.880
That's why I...

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:23.410
That song sounded like it was
coming down from the sky!

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:30.730
But I guess once an omiso,
always an omiso.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.360
Kanata.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:37.720
We can't just rely on the
church for everything.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.700
The Takemikazuchi is a
relic from a past era.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:45.830
And a lot of things are
sleeping inside it.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.090
A lot of things?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:51.250
Yeah. Ask Noël for the details.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.740
OK, this is it.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.280
Here goes!

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:20.740
This is it!

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.820
This song!

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.970
This is probably what that song
sounds like complete.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:10.050
Lots of instruments, all playing in harmony,
becoming one piece of music.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:12.970
It's the same as a tank crew.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:19.030
Commander, gunner, driver,
and communications...

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:22.820
Everyone works together
to operate one tank.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.540
Every part is important.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.350
Every sound is important.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:36.800
Don't look at me like that.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:38.320
It's just something I heard

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:43.060
from the person I respect and
admire more than anyone.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:51.140
To borrow her words...
Kanata, why do you think superior officers exist?

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:55.250
So their juniors can cause
problems for them.

00:20:57.890 --> 00:20:59.570
It's fine if you can't do it now.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:02.660
Just remember how much it hurt,
how powerless it felt,

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:05.510
and how happy you were
to be protected.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:12.230
And someday, when you're in the position
to protect someone, it will help you.

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:17.550
So cause as much trouble
for me as you'd like.

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:19.730
I did the same.

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:24.000
Of course, if you screw up,
you'll be scolded and punished.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:27.090
But... If it hurts, say so.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:28.260
When you're suffering, tell me.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:30.840
OK?

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:38.430
Understood!

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:42.850
I'll make sure to cause lots and
lots of trouble for you!

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:45.050
N-Not that...

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.830
Go easy on me, OK?

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:59.340
Jeez... I should've stayed.

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:03.800
Kanata got Rio-sempai
to nurse her.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:06.880
What? It was no big deal.

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:08.930
Looks like she was just tired.

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:10.800
She'll be fine if she sleeps.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:19.040
The Takemikazuchi's lights were on.

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:22.800
Sorry. I used it a bit.

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:24.790
Was there a problem?

00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:28.640
You listened to that
song, didn't you?

00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:30.660
Yeah.

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:34.530
You said you never would again.

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:37.330
I just really wanted to hear it.

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:40.630
So?

00:22:42.690 --> 00:22:44.080
It's a secret.

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:19.930
Rainy Season Sky
- Quartz Rainbow

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:17.090
Next time:

00:24:17.090 --> 00:24:19.330
Rainy Season Sky,
Quartz Rainbow.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:24.980
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
